.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-INSPECT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-inspect - Show daemon-local HTTP captures


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel inspect <tunnel> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Read or manage the HTTP requests this machine's daemon captured for a tunnel. Name the
route with --route when the tunnel has several; filter with --id, and page with --cursor and
--limit (1-100, default 20). --enable and --disable turn capturing on or off, --purge deletes
the captured requests, and --body and --raw (bodies, exact requests for replay) apply only
together with --enable.

.PP
Captures can contain sensitive traffic such as tokens and personal data. Treat the output
accordingly.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP[=false]
	capture request/response bodies with --enable

.PP
\fB--cursor\fP=""
	continue after a capture cursor

.PP
\fB--disable\fP[=false]
	disable capture for this resource

.PP
\fB--enable\fP[=false]
	enable capture for this resource

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for inspect

.PP
\fB--id\fP=""
	show one capture by ID

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=20
	maximum captures per request (1-100)

.PP
\fB--purge\fP[=false]
	purge retained captures for this resource

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	retain exact raw requests for replay with --enable

.PP
\fB--route\fP=""
	inspect one route ID (required when the tunnel has several routes)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel inspect web --limit 10
  pb tunnel inspect web --route route_xyz --id cap_123
  pb tunnel inspect web --enable --body
  pb tunnel inspect web --purge
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
